{
 "_comment": "One table from a creature look to a body (view/actors/looks.gd). Resolution: a monster-forge GLB when assets/monsters/<slug> is synced; else the row for the slug / people key / player key (keys fall back by dropping their last ':' part, so people:elf:drow:raider -> people:elf:drow -> people:elf); else by_type (creature type from data/looks_creatures.json), then default. A row names a model; when its files are not fetched the actor is a tinted primitive with a nameplate, sized by by_size. Rows: model (a key of models), size_name (the box size when the look has no slug: people:goblin is small), tint (hex, multiplies colours), height_m (overrides the model's height), scale (multiplies it), nameplate (true: show the name), color (primitive colour). models: path (res:// literal, so tools/fetch_assets.sh fetches it), show (mesh node names to keep in a multi-character file), set (masc | femn: which locomotion clips; omitted = not a humanoid, no retargeting), height_m (the model is scaled to this height; people are scaled to their box otherwise), clip (static models: play the file's own animation). Synty supplies looks only: every key is an SRD slug, an SRD species/role, or a class.",
