 "swings": {
  "_comment": "How bodies swing (view/actors/swing_plan.gd). clips: a name for each file; retargeted on first use, and only the span the moves use is sampled. moves: pre [clip, from_s, contact_s] is stretched over the wind-up (a combo's follow-up: over its gap), post [clip, contact_s, to_s] over the rest of the action, so the tip of the blade peaks exactly at the host's contact whatever the tempo; those times were chosen by eye on tools/clip_sheet.gd (tools/clip_probe.gd finds the blade's fastest moment, which is often the backswing). tempo: for each class of data/combat.json weapon_tempo, the moves consecutive swings walk through. upper_from: the bones from which a body keeps swinging while its legs run. Synty's combo clips are sections of one take: before from_s they only hold a pose, and the ReturnToIdle files have no swing in them at all.",
